Third-party software
--------------------

Coxia's packages bundle open-source components (the Electron runtime, React,
Mermaid, electron-updater, the IBM Plex fonts and their dependencies), each
under its own license. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists the production
dependencies with their versions and licenses, and flags the ones that are not
under a permissive license. Regenerate it with:

    node scripts/third-party-notices.mjs

The Claude Agent SDK is proprietary software of Anthropic, PBC, governed by
Anthropic's terms. It is NOT part of the public Coxia packages and is not
redistributed by this project; the setup wizard installs it on the user's
machine after showing the terms. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The optional voice feature installs Python packages and speech models on the
user's machine at the user's request (sidecar/requirements.txt). They are not
distributed with Coxia; their licenses are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
